<% content_for :title, 'Replace star system' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Replace Star System' do %>
  <div class='space-y-6'>
    <div class='space-y-3 text-fg'>
      <p>
        The replace operation destroys the existing star system — all stars, orbital bodies,
        and rogue objects in the parsec — and constructs a new one in its place.
        This action is irreversible. Systems marked as locked cannot be replaced.
      </p>
      <p>
        Enter a name, select an initialisation mode, and press
        <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Replace</span> to execute.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='font-semibold text-highlight mb-2'>Initialisation modes</p>

      <dl class='space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Empty</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Constructs a star system with no orbital bodies. When this mode is selected you
            configure the primary star by choosing a spectral type, subtype, and luminosity class.
            A primary star is required for a star system.
          </dd>
          <dd class='mt-2 text-fg'>
            Use this when the replacement system has a known stellar configuration that must be
            entered manually.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Random</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Generates a fully populated star system with stars, orbital bodies, and a main world.
            Enable the <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Populated</span> option to ensure
            the generated main world carries a population.
          </dd>
          <dd class='mt-2 text-fg'>
            Use this when a complete replacement system is needed and its composition does not
            require manual specification.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Build configuration</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Accepts a YAML directive packet that instructs the generator how to construct the
            replacement system. Permits specification of the primary star and companions, orbital
            body density, allegiance, bases, and individual bodies with specific UWP codes.
          </dd>
          <dd class='mt-2 text-fg'>
            Use this when the replacement must conform to known parameters. See the
            <%= link_to 'star system build specification',
                        help_page_path('star_system_build_specification'),
                        class: 'hover:underline underline-offset-4' %>
            for the full YAML reference.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='font-semibold text-highlight mb-2'>Derive Build from Survey</p>

      <div class='space-y-3 text-fg'>
        <p>
          The <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Derive Build from Survey</span> button
          reads the current system's stars and orbital bodies and produces a YAML build
          configuration that approximates that composition. The derived configuration is written
          into the build configuration field and may be edited before the replacement is executed.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is useful when re-generating a system that has drifted from its original
          specification, or when a hand-built system must be seeded back through the generator
          to populate missing fields.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='font-semibold text-highlight mb-2'>Primary star fields (Empty mode)</p>

      <dl class='space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Type</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The spectral type of the star: O, B, A, F, G, K, or M. Special types
            (Brown Dwarf, White Dwarf, Black Hole, Pulsar, Neutron Star) are also available.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Subtype</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            A digit from 0 to 9 that refines the spectral type. Lower numbers are hotter
            within the class. Not required for special types.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Luminosity class</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The size classification of the star, from Ia (luminous supergiant) through VI
            (subdwarf). Main sequence stars are class V. Not required for special types.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0619RS
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>